{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-148e28a0-ae53-4d06-be4e-525a81f3b095-18\nfc_eb19fab6-e132-92f8-abca-89b3ce8f01c7_2","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"# Find loom data / critic feedback\nwhich loom 2>/dev/null; loom data show MARATHON-18 --output json 2>/dev/null | head -c 8000; ls /work/ws/sessions/ | rg -i 'critic|frontend|backend' | tail -30","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-148e28a0-ae53-4d06-be4e-525a81f3b095-18\nfc_eb19fab6-e132-92f8-abca-89b3ce8f01c7_2","simpleCommands":["which","loom","head","ls","rg","tail"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"which","args":[{"type":"word","value":"loom"}],"fullText":"which loom"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-18"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-18 --output json"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"number","value":"8000"}],"fullText":"head -c 8000"},{"name":"ls","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/sessions/"}],"fullText":"ls /work/ws/sessions/"},{"name":"rg","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-i"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'critic|frontend|backend'"}],"fullText":"rg -i 'critic|frontend|backend'"},{"name":"tail","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-30"}],"fullText":"tail -30"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Fetch loom task MARATHON-18 state","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"a42df522-cd26-417c-87e5-65513de2eb14","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"# Find loom data / critic feedback\nwhich loom 2>/dev/null; loom data show MARATHON-18 --output json 2>/dev/null | head -c 8000; ls /work/ws/sessions/ | rg -i 'critic|frontend|backend' | tail -30","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-18\",\n  \"title\": \"SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"frontend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-18 — SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the epic’s stable DOM ids plus `settings-*` / `invitation-*` / role / channel-member `data-testid`s so CUA/Playwright can drive admin flows at 1280×900. It also specifies the missing **channel add-member** REST seam that MARATHON-7 deferred, because the channel-settings “add” control cannot work against join alone for private channels.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\\n| Module split | New `static/js/settings_ui.js` owns both modals; `shell.js` exposes open triggers + active workspace/channel; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\\n| Modal pattern | Match `auth-modal`: overlay + panel, `hidden` attribute, `role=\\\"dialog\\\"`, Escape/close dismiss; **one settings modal open at a time** |\\n| Workspace entry | `data-testid=\\\"workspace-settings-btn\\\"` in `workspace-header` (visible whenever shell shows a workspace) |\\n| Channel entry | Selecting a non-DM channel in `channel-list` sets active channel; `data-testid=\\\"channel-settings-btn\\\"` in message-pane header chrome (or beside channel list) opens channel settings for that id — **does not** require MARATHON-17 message composer |\\n| Tabs | Workspace modal: exactly three tabs — `general`, `members`, `invitations`; only one panel visible |\\n| Authz UX | Client **hides/disables** privileged controls from cached caller role; server remains SoT (403/404 still shown as `error.message`) |\\n| Invitation redeem | Onboarding gains an **accept-by-code** form (M12 assigned redeem UX to this task); settings tab is create/list/revoke only |\\n| Channel add-member | New backend seam `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (this design owns the contract); frontend labeled implementer may land the thin route or a tiny backend follow-up must land first — see Sequencing |\\n| Selectors | Exact strings below; prefer `data-testid`; required **DOM ids**: `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Epic requires settings + invitations in the SPA with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred settings modals here.\\n- Backend contracts for name/join_mode, roles, invitations, topic, archive, channel member list are closed (M6/7/12); inventing alternate envelopes would break graders and sibling designs.\\n- M7’s neighborhood note already flagged `channel-add-member-*` without REST — shipping UI without an add seam leaves private-channel “add” untestable.\\n- Keeping vanilla modules preserves `start.sh` / no-Node ops.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Fold settings into MARATHON-17 message chrome only | Blocks settings QA until messages land; task is independent with `frontend` label |\\n| “Add member” = tell user to `POST .../join` | Fails for private channels (403 without membership); hooks expect add controls |\\n| Profile PATCH inside General tab | Task tabs are name/join_mode/members/invitations only; profile is a different surface |\\n| Groups CRUD UI | MARATHON-12 groups API exists but is not in this task description |\\n| React settings app | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nChannel add-member needs a **small backend POST** that did not ship in M7. This design locks that seam so SPA and server can be implemented in parallel; if the implementer is frontend-only, the lead should keep `frontend` and optionally add a short backend subtask — **do not** fake add via SQL in the browser.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: vanilla SPA; `api()` + bearer; `{error:{code,message}}`; visible form errors; `hidden` for unused chrome; hash `#/w/{slug}`; token keys unchanged.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: `WorkspaceObj` keys `{id,slug,name,owner_id,join_mode}`; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; `MemberObj` `{user_id,role,username,display_name}`; roles `owner|admin|member|guest`; non-member → 404; privilege → 403; PATCH workspace name/join_mode; PATCH member role matrix; `POST .../transfer_ownership`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys; `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → `{members: UserObj[]}`; `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}`; `POST .../archive` / `.../unarchive` owner-only; archived topic writes → **423** `archived`; leave/join exist but settings “add” is not join.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-12**: `InvitationObj`; create/list/revoke/accept envelopes; invite_only join still 403 without accept.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3/4**: `UserObj` keys on channel members list; bearer auth.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\\n\\nAll names are **`data-testid` values** unless noted as **DOM `id`**. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Product “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the table below is **normative** for this task and matches the task wording (`settings-*`, `invitation-*`, role/channel-member names from sibling designs).\\n\\n#### Required DOM ids\\n\\n| `id` | Element |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `workspace-settings-modal` | Workspace settings overlay/dialog root |\\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Channel settings overlay/dialog root |\\n| `create-invitation-form` | Form that creates a workspace invitation |\\n\\nAlso set matching `data-testid` equal to the id string for the three roots/forms above (so either selector style works).\\n\\n#### Open / chrome\\n\\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\\n|---------------|--------------|------|\\n| `workspace-settings-btn` | Shell with current workspace | Opens workspace settings modal |\\n| `channel-settings-btn` | Shell with an active non-DM channel | Opens channel settings for that channel |\\n| `workspace-settings-close` | Workspace modal open | Closes workspace modal |\\n| `channel-settings-close` | Channel modal open | Closes channel modal |\\n\\n#### Workspace settings — tabs \\u0026 general\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Role |\\n|---------------|------|\\n| `settings-tab-general` | Selects General tab |\\n| `settings-tab-members` | Selects Members tab |\\n| `settings-tab-invitations` | Selects Invitations tab |\\n| `settings-panel-general` | General panel region |\\n| `settings-panel-members` | Members panel region |\\n| `settings-panel-invitations` | Invitations panel region |\\n| `settings-name` | Workspace display name `\\u003cinput\\u003e` |\\n| `settings-join-mode` | `\\u003cselect\\u003e` or radio group; values `open` \\\\| `invite_only` |\\n| `settings-general-save` | Submit/save general settings |\\n| `settings-general-error` | Visible error text for general save failures |\\n| `settings-general-success` | Optional brief success indicator (may be aria-live); not required if save is silently successful and fields reflect server |\\n\\n**Negative:** Member/guest must **not** successfully persist general changes; controls may be disabled **or** save shows `settings-general-error` with server `error.message` (403).\\n\\n#### Workspace settings — members\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Role |\\n|---------------|------|\\n| `settings-members-list` | Container for member rows |\\n| `settings-member-ro20260822-222319-backend-dev-1--99c51c28\n20260822-223733-backend-dev-1--b08fae58\n20260822-225356-backend-dev-1--2f8554e2\n20260822-230008-backend-dev-1--cfebd2ac\n20260822-232925-frontend-dev-1--22b12422\n20260822-233543-backend-dev-1--5fd5e7e5\n20260823-000220-backend-dev-1--f428556a\n20260823-001419-backend-dev-1--5794d074\n20260823-004058-backend-dev-1--5fe648b0\n20260823-004658-frontend-dev-1--544cf7f4\n20260823-005857-backend-dev-1--384493f5\n20260823-011144-frontend-dev-1--151527d5\n20260823-011456-backend-dev-1--6271d23a\n","stderr":"","executionTime":108,"interleavedOutput":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-18\",\n  \"title\": \"SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"frontend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-18 — SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the epic’s stable DOM ids plus `settings-*` / `invitation-*` / role / channel-member `data-testid`s so CUA/Playwright can drive admin flows at 1280×900. It also specifies the missing **channel add-member** REST seam that MARATHON-7 deferred, because the channel-settings “add” control cannot work against join alone for private channels.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\\n| Module split | New `static/js/settings_ui.js` owns both modals; `shell.js` exposes open triggers + active workspace/channel; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\\n| Modal pattern | Match `auth-modal`: overlay + panel, `hidden` attribute, `role=\\\"dialog\\\"`, Escape/close dismiss; **one settings modal open at a time** |\\n| Workspace entry | `data-testid=\\\"workspace-settings-btn\\\"` in `workspace-header` (visible whenever shell shows a workspace) |\\n| Channel entry | Selecting a non-DM channel in `channel-list` sets active channel; `data-testid=\\\"channel-settings-btn\\\"` in message-pane header chrome (or beside channel list) opens channel settings for that id — **does not** require MARATHON-17 message composer |\\n| Tabs | Workspace modal: exactly three tabs — `general`, `members`, `invitations`; only one panel visible |\\n| Authz UX | Client **hides/disables** privileged controls from cached caller role; server remains SoT (403/404 still shown as `error.message`) |\\n| Invitation redeem | Onboarding gains an **accept-by-code** form (M12 assigned redeem UX to this task); settings tab is create/list/revoke only |\\n| Channel add-member | New backend seam `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (this design owns the contract); frontend labeled implementer may land the thin route or a tiny backend follow-up must land first — see Sequencing |\\n| Selectors | Exact strings below; prefer `data-testid`; required **DOM ids**: `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Epic requires settings + invitations in the SPA with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred settings modals here.\\n- Backend contracts for name/join_mode, roles, invitations, topic, archive, channel member list are closed (M6/7/12); inventing alternate envelopes would break graders and sibling designs.\\n- M7’s neighborhood note already flagged `channel-add-member-*` without REST — shipping UI without an add seam leaves private-channel “add” untestable.\\n- Keeping vanilla modules preserves `start.sh` / no-Node ops.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| Fold settings into MARATHON-17 message chrome only | Blocks settings QA until messages land; task is independent with `frontend` label |\\n| “Add member” = tell user to `POST .../join` | Fails for private channels (403 without membership); hooks expect add controls |\\n| Profile PATCH inside General tab | Task tabs are name/join_mode/members/invitations only; profile is a different surface |\\n| Groups CRUD UI | MARATHON-12 groups API exists but is not in this task description |\\n| React settings app | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nChannel add-member needs a **small backend POST** that did not ship in M7. This design locks that seam so SPA and server can be implemented in parallel; if the implementer is frontend-only, the lead should keep `frontend` and optionally add a short backend subtask — **do not** fake add via SQL in the browser.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: vanilla SPA; `api()` + bearer; `{error:{code,message}}`; visible form errors; `hidden` for unused chrome; hash `#/w/{slug}`; token keys unchanged.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: `WorkspaceObj` keys `{id,slug,name,owner_id,join_mode}`; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; `MemberObj` `{user_id,role,username,display_name}`; roles `owner|admin|member|guest`; non-member → 404; privilege → 403; PATCH workspace name/join_mode; PATCH member role matrix; `POST .../transfer_ownership`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys; `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → `{members: UserObj[]}`; `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}`; `POST .../archive` / `.../unarchive` owner-only; archived topic writes → **423** `archived`; leave/join exist but settings “add” is not join.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-12**: `InvitationObj`; create/list/revoke/accept envelopes; invite_only join still 403 without accept.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3/4**: `UserObj` keys on channel members list; bearer auth.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\\n\\nAll names are **`data-testid` values** unless noted as **DOM `id`**. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Product “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the table below is **normative** for this task and matches the task wording (`settings-*`, `invitation-*`, role/channel-member names from sibling designs).\\n\\n#### Required DOM ids\\n\\n| `id` | Element |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `workspace-settings-modal` | Workspace settings overlay/dialog root |\\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Channel settings overlay/dialog root |\\n| `create-invitation-form` | Form that creates a workspace invitation |\\n\\nAlso set matching `data-testid` equal to the id string for the three roots/forms above (so either selector style works).\\n\\n#### Open / chrome\\n\\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\\n|---------------|--------------|------|\\n| `workspace-settings-btn` | Shell with current workspace | Opens workspace settings modal |\\n| `channel-settings-btn` | Shell with an active non-DM channel | Opens channel settings for that channel |\\n| `workspace-settings-close` | Workspace modal open | Closes workspace modal |\\n| `channel-settings-close` | Channel modal open | Closes channel modal |\\n\\n#### Workspace settings — tabs \\u0026 general\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Role |\\n|---------------|------|\\n| `settings-tab-general` | Selects General tab |\\n| `settings-tab-members` | Selects Members tab |\\n| `settings-tab-invitations` | Selects Invitations tab |\\n| `settings-panel-general` | General panel region |\\n| `settings-panel-members` | Members panel region |\\n| `settings-panel-invitations` | Invitations panel region |\\n| `settings-name` | Workspace display name `\\u003cinput\\u003e` |\\n| `settings-join-mode` | `\\u003cselect\\u003e` or radio group; values `open` \\\\| `invite_only` |\\n| `settings-general-save` | Submit/save general settings |\\n| `settings-general-error` | Visible error text for general save failures |\\n| `settings-general-success` | Optional brief success indicator (may be aria-live); not required if save is silently successful and fields reflect server |\\n\\n**Negative:** Member/guest must **not** successfully persist general changes; controls may be disabled **or** save shows `settings-general-error` with server `error.message` (403).\\n\\n#### Workspace settings — members\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Role |\\n|---------------|------|\\n| `settings-members-list` | Container for member rows |\\n| `settings-member-ro20260822-222319-backend-dev-1--99c51c28\n20260822-223733-backend-dev-1--b08fae58\n20260822-225356-backend-dev-1--2f8554e2\n20260822-230008-backend-dev-1--cfebd2ac\n20260822-232925-frontend-dev-1--22b12422\n20260822-233543-backend-dev-1--5fd5e7e5\n20260823-000220-backend-dev-1--f428556a\n20260823-001419-backend-dev-1--5794d074\n20260823-004058-backend-dev-1--5fe648b0\n20260823-004658-frontend-dev-1--544cf7f4\n20260823-005857-backend-dev-1--384493f5\n20260823-011144-frontend-dev-1--151527d5\n20260823-011456-backend-dev-1--6271d23a\n","localExecutionTimeMs":52},"isBackground":false},"description":"Fetch loom task MARATHON-18 state"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-148e28a0-ae53-4d06-be4e-525a81f3b095-18\nfc_eb19fab6-e132-92f8-abca-89b3ce8f01