MPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=6c6170f7b7fb6d4ccb358c5af71c7031f3d20512\", \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:00:18.495714294Z\"}\n{\"id\": 52, \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\", \"author\": \"marathon-harness\", \"text\": \"CRITIC REVIEW attempt=1 commit=6c6170f7b7fb6d4ccb358c5af71c7031f3d20512 CHANGES-REQUESTED \\u2014 Settings UI + POST /api/channels/{id}/members look complete, but the candidate deletes shipped DMs (/api/dms), channel message POST/GET, message edit/delete/replies/reactions, schema migration v5, and their tests \\u2014 unacceptable regressions vs base for an M18 settings task.\", \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:11:25.220114089Z\n{\"id\": 53, \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\", \"author\": \"marathon-harness\", \"text\": \"FEEDBACK attempt=1: critic requested changes; see CRITIC comment\", \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:11:25.418295744Z\"}\n{\"id\": 54, \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\", \"author\": \"backend-dev-1\", \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=2 commit=dd755ee3bded705073c452cf0132601e5e8aa2e9\", \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:17:00.983233058Z\"}\nnotes: REBASE: cherry-picked prior IMPL 6c6170f onto HEAD with M8/M9 (messages + /api/dms + schema v5) preserved; conflict resolved in server/channels/routes.py keeping PostMessageBody and AddChannelMemberBody. 220 tests green.\n489 /tmp/m18-design.md\n5:This task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the epic’s stable DOM ids plus `settings-*` / `invitation-*` / role / channel-member `data-testid`s so CUA/Playwright can drive admin flows at 1280×900. It also specifies the missing **channel add-member** REST seam that MARATHON-7 deferred, because the channel-settings “add” control cannot work against join alone for private channels.\n16:| Workspace entry | `data-testid=\"workspace-settings-btn\"` in `workspace-header` (visible whenever shell shows a workspace) |\n17:| Channel entry | Selecting a non-DM channel in `channel-list` sets active channel; `data-testid=\"channel-settings-btn\"` in message-pane header chrome (or beside channel list) opens channel settings for that id — **does not** require MARATHON-17 message composer |\n21:| Channel add-member | New backend seam `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (this design owns the contract); frontend labeled implementer may land the thin route or a tiny backend follow-up must land first — see Sequencing |\n22:| Selectors | Exact strings below; prefer `data-testid`; required **DOM ids**: `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` |\n28:- M7’s neighborhood note already flagged `channel-add-member-*` without REST — shipping UI without an add seam leaves private-channel “add” untestable.\n36:| “Add member” = tell user to `POST .../join` | Fails for private channels (403 without membership); hooks expect add controls |\n43:Channel add-member needs a **small backend POST** that did not ship in M7. This design locks that seam so SPA and server can be implemented in parallel; if the implementer is frontend-only, the lead should keep `frontend` and optionally add a short backend subtask — **do not** fake add via SQL in the browser.\n49:From **MARATHON-5/6**: `WorkspaceObj` keys `{id,slug,name,owner_id,join_mode}`; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; `MemberObj` `{user_id,role,username,display_name}`; roles `owner|admin|member|guest`; non-member → 404; privilege → 403; PATCH workspace name/join_mode; PATCH member role matrix; `POST .../transfer_ownership`.\n51:From **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys; `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → `{members: UserObj[]}`; `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}`; `POST .../archive` / `.../unarchive` owner-only; archived topic writes → **423** `archived`; leave/join exist but settings “add” is not join.\n61:All names are **`data-testid` values** unless noted as **DOM `id`**. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Product “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the table below is **normative** for this task and matches the task wording (`settings-*`, `invitation-*`, role/channel-member names from sibling designs).\n71:Also set matching `data-testid` equal to the id string for the three roots/forms above (so either selector style works).\n75:| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n84:| `data-testid` | Role |\n102:| `data-testid` | Role |\n121:| `data-testid` | Role |\n141:| `data-testid` | Role |\n150:| `data-testid` | Role |\n161:| `channel-add-member-input` | Username or user id input for add |\n162:| `channel-add-member-submit` | Add submit |\n163:| `channel-add-member-error` | Add error |\n204:### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/transfer_ownership`\n215:#### Create — `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **201** `{invitation}`\n237:#### Accept — `POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept` → **200** `{workspace, channels?, read_state?}`\n251:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` | Owner; on 200 set local `is_archived=true`, swap buttons, refresh shell channel list if archived channels are hidden by default |\n252:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/unarchive` | Owner; opposite |\n258:### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (**new**; owned by this design)\n265:POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/members\n292:**Client:** submit `channel-add-member-input` as username (trim); disable submit in flight; on 200 replace list; on 4xx show `channel-add-member-error`.\n325:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | **No DDL** — uses existing `channel_members` (v2). Backward compatible additive route |\n338:| `tests/test_spa_settings.py` | TestClient: HTML contains required ids/testids; static JS references key API paths; optional smoke that create_app still serves `/` |\n345:| `static/index.html` | Add both modals (hidden), invitation accept form in onboarding, workspace/channel settings buttons hooks; all required testids/ids in markup (rows may be JS-generated but modal chrome + forms must be present for SPA shell tests) |\n349:| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | Extend `REQUIRED_TESTIDS` (or sibling list) with stable settings chrome ids that must appear in initial HTML (`workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form`, tab testids, invitation-accept-*) |\n350:| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST /{channel_id}/members` per contract above |\n366:1. HTML modal shells + CSS + required testids (unblocks selector tests).\n376:- Add-member UI blocked on `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` implementation (same PR or tiny backend follow-up).\n383:| Settings / invitation / role / channel-member `data-testid` set | QA / CUA |\n384:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | SPA channel settings; future slash invites |\n409:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` as substitute for add-member | existing join route | Wrong authz for private add; out of scope as the add mechanism |\n419:| `server/channels/routes.py` GET members / PATCH / archive | **Consume**; add POST members |\n424:| M7 note `channel-add-member-*` | **In scope** via new POST + testids |\n446:| Add member unknown username | 400 → `channel-add-member-error` |\n455:## Acceptance Criteria\n457:1. `GET /` HTML includes DOM ids `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` and the normative `data-testid`s listed above for modal chrome, tabs, general fields, invitation accept form, and channel settings fields (list rows may be empty until data loads).\n474:- Extend/add TestClient tests asserting required ids/testids in `GET /` and that `settings_ui.js` is served as a static asset.\n475:- Backend tests for `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` matrix (owner/admin/member/guest, private/public, idempotent, DM rejection, non-member target).\n484:5. Create private channel (API or future M17 UI) → add workspace member via `channel-add-member-*` → member appears in list.\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T01:18:04.307Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":121,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T01:18:04.307Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ndesign len 28511\n## Acceptance 25233\n### Acceptance -1\n## Interface 5052\n### Channel add-member -1\nPOST /api/channels 2175\n## Sequencing 19712\n## Out of scope -1\n--- comments ---\n{\"id\": 44, \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\", \"author\": \"marathon-harness\", \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=23\", \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:46:55.156906883Z\"}\n{\"id\": 46, \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\", \"author\": \"frontend-dev-1\", \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=6c6170f7b7fb6d4ccb358c5af71c7031f3d20512\", \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:00:18.495714294Z\"}\n{\"id\": 52, \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\", \"author\": \"marathon-harness\", \"text\": \"CRITIC REVIEW attempt=1 commit=6c6170f7b7fb6d4ccb358c5af71c7031f3d20512 CHANGES-REQUESTED \\u2014 Settings UI + POST /api/channels/{id}/members look complete, but the candidate deletes shipped DMs (/api/dms), channel message POST/GET, message edit/delete/replies/reactions, schema migration v5, and their tests \\u2014 unacceptable regressions vs base for an M18 settings task.\", \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:11:25.220114089Z\n{\"id\": 53, \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\", \"author\": \"marathon-harness\", \"text\": \"FEEDBACK attempt=1: critic requested changes; see CRITIC comment\", \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:11:25.418295744Z\"}\n{\"id\": 54, \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\", \"author\": \"backend-dev-1\", \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=2 commit=dd755ee3bded705073c452cf0132601e5e8aa2e9\", \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T01:17:00.983233058Z\"}\nnotes: REBASE: cherry-picked prior IMPL 6c6170f onto HEAD with M8/M9 (messages + /api/dms + schema v5) preserved; conflict resolved in server/channels/routes.py keeping PostMessageBody and AddChannelMemberBody. 220 tests green.\n489 /tmp/m18-design.md\n5:This task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the epic’s stable DOM ids plus `settings-*` / `invitation-*` / role / channel-member `data-testid`s so CUA/Playwright can drive admin flows at 1280×900. It also specifies the missing **channel add-member** REST seam that MARATHON-7 deferred, because the channel-settings “add” control cannot work against join alone for private channels.\n16:| Workspace entry | `data-testid=\"workspace-settings-btn\"` in `workspace-header` (visible whenever shell shows a workspace) |\n17:| Channel entry | Selecting a non-DM channel in `channel-list` sets active channel; `data-testid=\"channel-settings-btn\"` in message-pane header chrome (or beside channel list) opens channel settings for that id — **does not** require MARATHON-17 message composer |\n21:| Channel add-member | New backend seam `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (this design owns the contract); frontend labeled implementer may land the thin route or a tiny backend follow-up must land first — see Sequencing |\n22:| Selectors | Exact strings below; prefer `data-testid`; required **DOM ids**: `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` |\n28:- M7’s neighborhood note already flagged `channel-add-member-*` without REST — shipping UI without an add seam leaves private-channel “add” untestable.\n36:| “Add member” = tell us