POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **201** `{invitation}`\n237:#### Accept — `POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept` → **200** `{workspace, channels?, read_state?}`\n251:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` | Owner; on 200 set local `is_archived=true`, swap buttons, refresh shell channel list if archived channels are hidden by default |\n252:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/unarchive` | Owner; opposite |\n258:### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (**new**; owned by this design)\n265:POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/members\n292:**Client:** submit `channel-add-member-input` as username (trim); disable submit in flight; on 200 replace list; on 4xx show `channel-add-member-error`.\n325:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | **No DDL** — uses existing `channel_members` (v2). Backward compatible additive route |\n338:| `tests/test_spa_settings.py` | TestClient: HTML contains required ids/testids; static JS references key API paths; optional smoke that create_app still serves `/` |\n345:| `static/index.html` | Add both modals (hidden), invitation accept form in onboarding, workspace/channel settings buttons hooks; all required testids/ids in markup (rows may be JS-generated but modal chrome + forms must be present for SPA shell tests) |\n349:| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | Extend `REQUIRED_TESTIDS` (or sibling list) with stable settings chrome ids that must appear in initial HTML (`workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form`, tab testids, invitation-accept-*) |\n350:| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST /{channel_id}/members` per contract above |\n366:1. HTML modal shells + CSS + required testids (unblocks selector tests).\n376:- Add-member UI blocked on `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` implementation (same PR or tiny backend follow-up).\n383:| Settings / invitation / role / channel-member `data-testid` set | QA / CUA |\n384:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | SPA channel settings; future slash invites |\n409:| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` as substitute for add-member | existing join route | Wrong authz for private add; out of scope as the add mechanism |\n419:| `server/channels/routes.py` GET members / PATCH / archive | **Consume**; add POST members |\n424:| M7 note `channel-add-member-*` | **In scope** via new POST + testids |\n446:| Add member unknown username | 400 → `channel-add-member-error` |\n455:## Acceptance Criteria\n457:1. `GET /` HTML includes DOM ids `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` and the normative `data-testid`s listed above for modal chrome, tabs, general fields, invitation accept form, and channel settings fields (list rows may be empty until data loads).\n474:- Extend/add TestClient tests asserting required ids/testids in `GET /` and that `settings_ui.js` is served as a static asset.\n475:- Backend tests for `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` matrix (owner/admin/member/guest, private/public, idempotent, DM rejection, non-member target).\n484:5. Create private channel (API or future M17 UI) → add workspace member via `channel-add-member-*` → member appears in list.\n","localExecutionTimeMs":64},"isBackground":false},"description":"Dump full design and comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-30289fe8-6e1f-4f92-acc9-2f51d58fbd9e-19\nfc_e479c75f-84da-9ec0-9f29-f1228422ce76_0","startedAtMs":"1787447884236","completedAtMs":"1787447884360"},"model_call_id":"51cc01bb-5c2b-48d1-8a21-dc3abf5ea0b5-6-heww","session_id":"a42df522-cd26-417c-87e5-65513de2eb14","timestamp_ms":1787447884399}
