{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-bfd18c4d-e621-4250-96d7-0bca86893810-20\nfc_78990874-3784-9746-9e43-6e0b3581d3cd_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/m18-design.md","offset":250,"limit":250},"result":{"success":{"content":"| `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}` | Save from `settings-topic`; **423** → message in `settings-topic-error` and disable further topic edits until unarchived |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` | Owner; on 200 set local `is_archived=true`, swap buttons, refresh shell channel list if archived channels are hidden by default |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/unarchive` | Owner; opposite |\n\nNon-owner: hide `settings-archive` / `settings-unarchive` (or disable). Topic save allowed for channel member or workspace owner per M7; others show 403 in error region.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (**new**; owned by this design)\n\nMissing today (M7 out-of-scope). Required for channel settings add.\n\n**Request**\n\n```http\nPOST /api/channels/{channel_id}/members\nAuthorization: Bearer …\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{ \"username\": \"ada\" }\n```\n\nAlternate accepted field: `{ \"user_id\": \"<uuid>\" }`. If both sent, must resolve to the same user else **400**. Unknown keys ignored. Exactly one of `username` / `user_id` required.\n\n**Authz / rules**\n\n1. Unknown channel → **404**.\n2. Caller must be **workspace member**; else **404** (no leak).\n3. Caller must be workspace **owner or admin**, **or** an existing **channel member** with workspace role ∈ {owner, admin, member} — **guest cannot add** → **403**.\n4. Target user must be a **workspace member** → else **400** `validation_error` (cannot add outsiders via this route; use workspace invitations first).\n5. Private or public: INSERT into `channel_members` if missing; idempotent if already member → **200**.\n6. DM channels (`is_dm=true`): **403** (DM membership is MARATHON-9).\n7. Archived channel: add membership **allowed** (membership mgmt, not a 423 “write” like topic/pin) — consistent with leave-on-archived in M7.\n\n**Response 200**\n\n```json\n{ \"members\": [ /* UserObj[], same shape/order as GET members */ ] }\n```\n\n(Prefer full refreshed list so SPA can re-render without a second GET.)\n\n**Client:** submit `channel-add-member-input` as username (trim); disable submit in flight; on 200 replace list; on 4xx show `channel-add-member-error`.\n\n---\n\n### HTTP client rules\n\nReuse MARATHON-16 `api()`: JSON, bearer, 15s timeout, envelope parse, 401 → logout. Never invent cookies.\n\n### Modal UX rules\n\n1. Opening workspace settings closes channel settings (and vice versa).\n2. Backdrop click and Escape close the active modal without saving pending edits (except already-fired role PATCH / invitation create).\n3. Switching workspace (hash/list) closes both modals.\n4. Viewport: usable at **1280×900**; modal panel scrollable if members list is long.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser / in-memory (no SQLite migration required for SPA-only path)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` | Already in shell; General tab mutates via PATCH |\n| `callerRole` | string \\| null | From members list or inferred |\n| `workspaceMembers` | `MemberObj[]` | Settings cache |\n| `invitations` | `InvitationObj[]` | Admin cache |\n| `activeChannel` | `ChannelObj` \\| null | For channel settings |\n| `channelMembers` | `UserObj[]` | Channel settings cache |\n\n### Server schema\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| SPA-only selectors/HTML/JS | N/A — no schema |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | **No DDL** — uses existing `channel_members` (v2). Backward compatible additive route |\n\n### Entities (unchanged shapes)\n\n- `WorkspaceObj`, `MemberObj`, `InvitationObj`, `ChannelObj`, `UserObj` — exact keys per M5/6/7/12. **Do not** nest extra fields in settings payloads.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/js/settings_ui.js` | Workspace + channel modal controllers; tab switching; all settings API calls; role-select / invitation / topic / archive / add-member handlers; exports `initSettingsUi(ctx)` |\n| `tests/test_spa_settings.py` | TestClient: HTML contains required ids/testids; static JS references key API paths; optional smoke that create_app still serves `/` |\n| `tests/test_channel_add_member.py` | **If** backend route lands with this task: authz matrix, idempotent add, guest 403, non-workspace target 400, DM 403 |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | Add both modals (hidden), invitation accept form in onboarding, workspace/channel settings buttons hooks; all required testids/ids in markup (rows may be JS-generated but modal chrome + forms must be present for SPA shell tests) |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Modal/tab/list styles consistent with auth-modal; do not break 1280×900 shell |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Wire `workspace-settings-btn`; track `activeChannel` on channel-list click; expose getters (`getWorkspace`, `getActiveChannel`, `refreshWorkspaceDetail`, `enterWorkspace`) to settings module; mount invitation-accept form submit |\n| `static/js/app.js` | `initSettingsUi` after shell init |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | Extend `REQUIRED_TESTIDS` (or sibling list) with stable settings chrome ids that must appear in initial HTML (`workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form`, tab testids, invitation-accept-*) |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST /{channel_id}/members` per contract above |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Helper `add_channel_member` / reuse insert; list members after add |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/workspaces/**`, `server/invitations/**` | Contracts already ship; SPA consumes |\n| `server/db.py` migrations | No schema change |\n| `start.sh` / `timer.sh` | No build step |\n| Message composer / thread panel behavior | MARATHON-17 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. HTML modal shells + CSS + required testids (unblocks selector tests).\n2. `settings_ui.js` General tab → PATCH workspace.\n3. Members tab → GET/PATCH members + transfer.\n4. Invitations tab → create/list/revoke; onboarding accept form.\n5. Channel settings → topic/archive/members list.\n6. Channel add-member route + UI last (or parallel once contract fixed).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- SPA work can proceed against existing M6/7/12 APIs immediately.\n- Add-member UI blocked on `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` implementation (same PR or tiny backend follow-up).\n- Independent of MARATHON-17 messages **except** shared `channel-list` click / active channel — this task may set active channel for settings without opening thread panel.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| Settings / invitation / role / channel-member `data-testid` set | QA / CUA |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | SPA channel settings; future slash invites |\n| `initSettingsUi` / open-modal hooks | MARATHON-17 may call `openChannelSettings(channelId)` from message header |\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- **Requires closed:** MARATHON-16 (shell), MARATHON-6 (members), MARATHON-7 (channel topic/archive/members GET), MARATHON-12 (invitations).\n- **Does not require:** MARATHON-8/13/14/17.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not recreate existing tasks)\n\n- User groups settings UI → new task if needed (not this description).\n- Profile / `PATCH /api/users/me` UI → separate settings surface.\n- Channel leave button in settings → optional later; leave API exists (M7) but not required by this task text.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| Message composer, reactions, thread panel open | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Different SPA task |\n| User groups CRUD UI | `settings-*` could grow; `server/groups` | Not in MARATHON-18 description |\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` | M16 deferred “profile” vaguely to settings; **this** task’s General tab is workspace name/join_mode only |\n| Pins UI | `/api/channels/{id}/pins` | Channel settings text is members/topic/archive only |\n| WebSocket live member updates | MARATHON-13 | Poll/refetch on tab open is enough |\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 | Unrelated |\n| Changing invitation accept semantics / join_mode gates | `server/invitations/**`, `server/workspaces/routes.py` join | Already shipped; SPA consumes |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` as substitute for add-member | existing join route | Wrong authz for private add; out of scope as the add mechanism |\n| React/Vite migration | — | Conflicts with M16 |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `static/index.html`, `static/js/shell.js`, `static/js/app.js`, `static/css/app.css` | **In scope** — extend |\n| `static/js/api.js`, `storage.js`, `auth_ui.js` | **Reuse** — no contract change |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | **In scope** — extend required selectors |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` GET members / PATCH / archive | **Consume**; add POST members |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` PATCH/members/transfer | **Consume only** |\n| `server/invitations/routes.py` | **Consume only** |\n| `tests/test_workspace_members.py`, `test_invitations.py`, `test_channels.py` | **Out of scope** to rewrite; keep green; add new tests |\n| Grep `settings-` / `invitation-` in `static/` | No hits yet — greenfield UI |\n| M7 note `channel-add-member-*` | **In scope** via new POST + testids |\n| Groups package | **Out of scope** UI |\n| `server/events.py` | **Out of scope** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Open workspace settings without admin role | Modal opens; General fields disabled or save → 403 visible; Members badge-only; Invitations admin-only empty/error |\n| PATCH general with blank name | Client may pre-check; server **400** → `settings-general-error` |\n| Invalid join_mode option | Must not be choosable in UI; if forced, server 400 |\n| Role select to `owner` | **Must not** be an option |\n| Admin tries to demote another admin | No select **or** PATCH 403 → revert + error |\n| Transfer to non-admin | Client only lists admins; server 400 if forced |\n| Create invitation as member | 403 → `invitation-create-error`; modal stays open |\n| Revoke already-used/expired code | 404 → refresh list (row disappears) |\n| Accept invalid/expired code | 404 → `invitation-accept-error`; stay on onboarding |\n| Accept targeted invite as wrong user | 403 → visible error |\n| Accept success while already member | 200 → enter workspace (idempotent) |\n| Topic save on archived channel | 423 → `settings-topic-error`; suggest unarchive |\n| Archive by non-owner | Control hidden/disabled; if called, 403 error |\n| Archive `#general` | Allowed if owner (server permits); UI does not special-case unless server errors |\n| Add member unknown username | 400 → `channel-add-member-error` |\n| Add member who is not workspace member | 400 → same |\n| Add to DM channel | Button hidden for `is_dm`; if called, 403 |\n| Add when already member | 200; list unchanged except refresh |\n| Network timeout | Visible error on active form; re-enable controls |\n| 401 on any settings call | Clear tokens; show auth modal; close settings |\n| Double-click save | Disable control until response; single in-flight request |\n| Modal open during workspace switch | Close modals; drop stale channel id |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET /` HTML includes DOM ids `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` and the normative `data-testid`s listed above for modal chrome, tabs, general fields, invitation accept form, and channel settings fields (list rows may be empty until data loads).\n2. Authenticated owner/admin can open workspace settings, change **name** and **join_mode**, save, and see updates in `workspace-header` / subsequent `GET` workspace detail.\n3. Member/guest **cannot** persist general settings (disabled UI and/or visible 403); must **not** silently succeed.\n4. Members tab lists all workspace members with `role-badge`; owner/admin can change permitted roles via `role-select`; forbidden changes show error and do **not** leave a lying UI role.\n5. Owner can transfer ownership to an admin via transfer controls; previous owner becomes admin in the refreshed list.\n6. Admin/owner can create an invitation; `invitation-code` is visible; list shows active invites; revoke removes the row.\n7. Onboarding `invitation-accept-*` redeems a valid code and enters the workspace shell; invite_only workspaces become accessible without using broken join-by-slug alone.\n8. With an active public/private channel, channel settings shows members (`channel-member-row`), allows topic save for authorized callers, and owner can archive/unarchive with UI reflecting `is_archived`.\n9. Topic save on archived channel surfaces **423** message and must **not** clear the topic field to empty on failure.\n10. Channel add-member with a workspace member username adds them to `channel_members` (UI list updates); guest cannot add; outsider username fails visibly.\n11. Opening one settings modal closes the other; logout closes modals and clears privileged data from the DOM on next login.\n12. Existing MARATHON-16 selectors and auth/workspace flows remain green (`tests/test_spa_shell.py` + prior SPA behavior).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/add TestClient tests asserting required ids/testids in `GET /` and that `settings_ui.js` is served as a static asset.\n- Backend tests for `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` matrix (owner/admin/member/guest, private/public, idempotent, DM rejection, non-member target).\n- Do **not** require a browser in unit CI; optional Playwright (as M16 notes) at 1280×900 for human/agent verification.\n\n### Manual / CUA script (1280×900)\n\n1. Register → create workspace → open workspace settings → rename + set `invite_only` → save → reload → values stick.\n2. Add second user via invitation create → copy `invitation-code` → logout → register other user → accept code → lands in workspace.\n3. As owner, change member role member→admin; confirm badge/select; attempt illegal admin-on-admin as admin user → error.\n4. Select `#general` → channel settings → set topic → archive → confirm topic save fails with archived error → unarchive → topic save works.\n5. Create private channel (API or future M17 UI) → add workspace member via `channel-add-member-*` → member appears in list.\n6. As guest/member, confirm invitations tab and archive controls are not usable.\n\n### Verification mindset\n\nOutside-in: selectors + REST envelopes + visible errors. No reliance on reading JS internals beyond confirming assets load.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":490,"fileSize":28740,"path":"/tmp/m18-design.md","readRange":{"startLine":250,"endLine":490},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-bfd18c4d-e621-4250-96d7-0bca86893810-20\nfc_78990874-3784-9746-9e43-6e0b3581d3cd_0","startedAtMs":"1787447887432","completedAtMs":"1787447889290"},"model_call_id":"51cc01bb-5c2b-48d1-8a21-dc3abf5ea0b5-7-fb1x","session_id":"a42df522-cd26-417c-87e5-65513de2eb14","timestamp_ms":1787447889395}
